From c880dca41e43d083db9a6de8e117505a2f7f08e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Morse Micro <support@morsemicro.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: lengthen the inter-transaction delay for non-block transfers

Taken verbatim from the Morse Micro OpenWrt feed, which is the vendor porting
template for this platform. The hash on the From line above is the real commit
that carries this patch in that feed (it is a feed commit, not a morse_driver
commit - upstream ships this file without a From line at all):
  repo   : https://github.com/MorseMicro/morse-feed
  commit : c880dca41e43d083db9a6de8e117505a2f7f08e9
           (pinned by github.com/MorseMicro/openwrt tag 3.0.2)
  path   : essentials/morse_driver/patches/mm61x/003_fix_spi_inter_transaction_delay.patch

Kept because the vendor applies it to the same driver revision this package
pins (mm6108-2.0.1). It replaces the local 003-ekh01-spi-fix.patch, whose own
inter-block delay change went the other way (flat delay instead of scaled) and
was written for the 1.11 era.

Original description from the vendor patch follows.

Add more delay between SPI transactions when not in block mode.
EKH01 in Openwrt has less delay between SPI transactions than Buildroot.
Currently the driver has enough delay between blocks but not when the transaction isn't a block.
Banff needs more delay than Eagle Crest, that's why this issue wasn't happening on Eagle Crest.

--- a/spi.c
+++ b/spi.c
@@ -577,7 +577,7 @@
 
 	if (!block) {
 		/* Scale bytes delay to block */
-		u32 extra_bytes = (count * mspi->inter_block_delay_bytes) / MMC_SPI_BLOCKSIZE;
+		u32 extra_bytes = max(250, (count * mspi->inter_block_delay_bytes) / MMC_SPI_BLOCKSIZE);
 
 		/* Allow 4 bytes for CRC and another 10 bytes for start block token & chip delays
 		 * (usually comes in 2).
@@ -709,7 +709,8 @@
 		if (block)
 			cp += mspi->inter_block_delay_bytes;
 		else
-			cp += spi_post_write_status_bytes;
+			/* stet: really we should use the new modparam here */
+			cp += max(250,(count * mspi->inter_block_delay_bytes) / MMC_SPI_BLOCKSIZE);
 	}
 
 	if (enable_ext_xtal_init) {
